A share that has used its budget exactly still has budget left.
It runs a tick more in every window than its budget allows;
a share has budget left while fewer ticks were charged to it than its part of the window.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a share waits on another queue than its budget says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ static void share_remove(struct share *s)
 /* Whether a share has budget left: fewer ticks charged in the window than its part of the window. */
 static bool share_owed(const struct share *s)
 {
-    return (uint64_t)s->used * BUDGET_WHOLE < (uint64_t)s->budget * WINDOW_TICKS;
+    return (uint64_t)s->used * BUDGET_WHOLE <= (uint64_t)s->budget * WINDOW_TICKS;
 }
 
 /* The queue a share waits on, as its threads, the turn, its budget and its flags now say; NULL for none. */
